---
---

<section class="card" aria-labelledby="h-brew">
  <div class="card-head">
    <h2 id="h-brew"><span class="step">2</span> Brew</h2>
    <p>Ratio stays locked. Change coffee and water follows; change water and coffee follows.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="suggest" id="suggest">
    <div class="suggest-top">
      <div>
        <span class="suggest-label">Suggested for this bean</span>
        <b class="mono" id="suggest-ratio">1:14</b>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="btn" id="btn-use-suggested">Use suggested</button>
    </div>
    <ul class="suggest-parts" id="suggest-parts"></ul>
    <p class="note">A starting point built from your 1:14 Kintamani test, not a lab result. Taste and adjust.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <label class="f" for="ratio">Ratio
      <span class="box" id="b-ratio"><span class="pre">1 :</span><input id="ratio" type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="0.5" min="4" max="30" /></span>
    </label>
    <label class="f" for="coffee">Coffee
      <span class="box" id="b-coffee"><input id="coffee" type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="1" min="0" /><span class="unit">g</span></span>
    </label>
    <label class="f" for="water">Water
      <span class="box" id="b-water"><input id="water" type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="10" min="0" /><span class="unit">ml</span></span>
    </label>
  </div>
  <p class="note" id="ratio-mode"></p>

  <div class="bloom-row">
    <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Bloom method" id="bloom-group">
      <button type="button" class="chip" id="bloom-room" data-bloom="false" aria-pressed="true">Room temperature</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" id="bloom-hot" data-bloom="true" aria-pressed="false">Hot bloom (90°C, 1.5× coffee weight)</button>
    </div>
    <details class="research inline">
      <summary>What the research says?</summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p><strong>Short answer: leave it off.</strong> Your no-bloom 40 g batch already hit the tea-like target, and nothing in the research argues for adding heat.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Warmer water extracts faster and pulls more acids and polyphenols. In one study, cold brew came out at pH 5.38 vs 5.18 for hot, with lower titratable acidity and fewer polyphenols.</li>
          <li>A hot bloom is a short hot extraction stacked on a cold one. Expect more brightness and aroma, and less of the smooth, low-acid cold brew character.</li>
          <li>Degassing, the usual reason to bloom, barely matters in a 12–14 hour immersion. The grounds end up fully wet either way.</li>
          <li>No peer-reviewed study tests a hot bloom in cold brew specifically. The table below is inference from the extraction data, not measured results.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="t">
            <thead><tr><th>Bean</th><th>Hot bloom likely does</th><th>Call</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Washed, high-grown (Yirgacheffe, Ají Bourbon)</td><td>More florals and acidity, less smooth</td><td>Optional. Try only if the brew is flat</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Washed, mid altitude (Kintamani)</td><td>Brighter citrus, less tea-like</td><td>Skip. Your test already works</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Honey</td><td>Slightly more sweetness and body</td><td>Skip</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Natural, fermented, co-fermented</td><td>Pushes boozy, winey ferment notes</td><td>Skip</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Wet-hulled, low altitude</td><td>More earthy bitterness</td><td>Skip</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="src">Sources: <a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2772502223000719" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Effects of grind size, temperature and brew ratio on cold brew (2023)</a> · <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-018-34392-w" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rao &amp; Fuller, Acidity and antioxidant activity of cold brew (2018)</a> · <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-017-18247-4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fuller &amp; Rao, Time, roast and grind in cold brew (2017)</a></p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <p class="warn" id="bloom-warn" hidden></p>

  <div class="out" aria-live="polite">
    <div id="o-bloom-wrap"><span>Hot bloom water</span><b id="o-bloom">–</b></div>
    <div><span id="o-rest-label">Room-temp water</span><b id="o-rest">–</b></div>
    <div><span>Absorbed by grounds</span><b id="o-absorbed">–</b></div>
    <div class="hl"><span>Expected yield</span><b id="o-yield">–</b></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note" id="effective-ratio" hidden></p>

  <ol class="steps" id="steps"></ol>
</section>

<style is:global>
  .suggest { border: 1.5px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .suggest-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .suggest-label { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
  .suggest b { font-size: 24px; color: var(--tea); }
  .suggest-parts { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 3px; font-size: 13px; }
  .suggest-parts li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 52px 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .suggest-parts .adj { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; text-align: right; }
  .suggest-parts .why { color: var(--muted); }
  .steps { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 4px; }
  .steps li::marker { color: var(--muted); font: 500 13px var(--font-mono); }
  .bloom-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px 16px; }
  .bloom-row .chips { flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .bloom-row details.research.inline { flex: 0 0 auto; max-width: 100%; }
  .bloom-row details.research.inline[open] { flex: 1 1 100%; }
</style>
